From: Steven Lee <steven_lee@aspeedtech.com>
Subject: [PATCH v1] hw/arm/aspeed_ast1040: Support FMC, stub SPI0/SPI1
 for ast1080 cs-group-analog-mux

Add a real aspeed.smc model for FMC (the actual boot flash) and its
w25q33pw flash chip. SPI0/SPI1 stay as unimplemented_device stubs
instead of getting the same real-model treatment: cs-group-analog-mux-
enable is an AST1080-only devicetree property (AST1040 has no SPI
filter/mux of its own) used by boards like ast1080_dcscm_bhs/oks to
alias CS0/CS1 and CS2/CS3 onto the same spi0/spi1 pins via an analog
mux, so the same flash window is legitimately programmed with what
looks like overlapping segments for the two CS groups. A real
aspeed.smc model doesn't know about the mux and treats this as an
invalid/overlapping segment ("aspeed_smc_flash_overlap"), which wedges
the boot before any console output ever appears - confirmed by
bisecting against the unimplemented-device stubs, where the same
firmware boots to the Zephyr banner and PFR state machine without
issue.

Signed-off-by: Steven Lee <steven_lee@aspeedtech.com>
